Ticket [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is not one failure repeated. Its reports describe two different
causes, so they need separate engineering issues.

## Parser: month-first parsing

The shared parser reads dates month first. Tenants whose locale writes day first can therefore get
the month and day swapped. This cause appears in reports from the app, email, and form channels.

## Hint: booking form format mismatch

The `booking-v3` form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` to people in day-first locales. Reports from that form
belong to a separate hint problem: the displayed format conflicts with the date convention those
tenants use.

## Classification and counts

The table applies the tenant locale and booking form rules to the merged reports. It removes
duplicate export rows by report ID; the intake tag is only an initial guess and does not determine
the cause. The one-day-move notes are evidence within the parser group, not a third cause.

